@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Server Info";
}

<section class="tc-page-hero tc-page-hero-server">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="tc-kicker">PLACEBO · ERA 1</div>
        <h1>Server Info</h1>
        <p>A clear reference for the rules, progression and systems that define Placebo.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="tc-serverinfo-shell">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="tc-server-summary">
            <div><span>Ruleset</span><strong>Era 1 · 5017 inspired</strong></div>
            <div><span>Client base</span><strong>5695 adapted</strong></div>
            <div><span>Level cap</span><strong>130</strong></div>
            <div><span>Market</span><strong>Physical Market</strong></div>
        </div>

        <div class="tc-section-heading mt-5">
            <div class="tc-kicker">CORE PROGRESSION</div>
            <h2>The classic foundation</h2>
            <p>Placebo targets the March 2008 Era 1 ruleset while retaining selected project-specific quality-of-life features.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="row tc-info-grid">
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-kept">Available</span>
                    <h3>Classic classes</h3>
                    <p>Trojan, Warrior, Archer, Fire Taoist and Water Taoist. Ninja is outside the Era 1 class roster.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-kept">Available</span>
                    <h3>Reborn</h3>
                    <p>Classic reborn progression remains part of the server, with character progression capped at level 130.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-kept">Available</span>
                    <h3>Nobility</h3>
                    <p>Nobility is retained as part of the Era 1 ruleset and its ranking remains available.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-kept">Available</span>
                    <h3>Guild War</h3>
                    <p>Classic guild competition remains a core part of Placebo, including persistent guild statues.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-kept">Project decision</span>
                    <h3>Arena</h3>
                    <p>Arena is later than the target patch, but is intentionally retained by the Placebo project.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-kept">Project decision</span>
                    <h3>Auto Hunt</h3>
                    <p>Auto Hunt is retained as quality of life. Auto Jump requires VIP 3+ and Auto Pick Up requires VIP 4+.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="tc-serverinfo-systems">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="tc-section-heading">
            <div class="tc-kicker">ERA BOUNDARIES</div>
            <h2>Systems intentionally disabled</h2>
            <p>Later progression layers are blocked so they cannot alter the intended Era 1 power curve or economy.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tc-system-table" role="table" aria-label="Placebo system availability">
            <div class="tc-system-row tc-system-head" role="row">
                <span>System</span><span>Status</span><span>Placebo rule</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Mounts</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Steeds, riding equipment and Riding/Spook/WarCry are blocked.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Clans</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Clan gameplay and Clan War are outside the Era 1 target.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Frozen Grotto</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Post-5017 Grotto maps are rejected by the server.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Talismans</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Fan and Tower progression is not part of Placebo Era 1.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Martial Arsenal</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Arsenal registration and its Battle Power contribution are removed.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Chi</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Chi progression and ranking are removed.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Sub-Class</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Sub-Class progression and related items are outside the ruleset.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Mentor / Apprentice</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>The later mentor system and mentor Battle Power are removed.</span></div>
            <div class="tc-system-row" role="row"><strong>Weapon accessories</strong><span class="tc-state-removed">Disabled</span><span>Later weapon-accessory equipment slots are blocked.</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="tc-serverinfo-shell">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-6 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-rule-panel">
                    <div class="tc-kicker">PK SYSTEM</div>
                    <h2>Classic PK consequences</h2>
                    <p>Red status begins at 30 PK Points and black status at 100. The later detained-item redemption system is not used: eligible equipment drops to the ground under the Era 1 rules.</p>
                    <div class="tc-rule-values">
                        <div><span>Kill common player</span><strong>+10 PK</strong></div>
                        <div><span>Kill personal enemy</span><strong>+5 PK</strong></div>
                        <div><span>Kill enemy guild member</span><strong>+3 PK</strong></div>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-6 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-rule-panel">
                    <div class="tc-kicker">ECONOMY</div>
                    <h2>Hunt, trade, progress</h2>
                    <p>The economy remains centered on hunting, Silver, Meteors, Dragon Balls, equipment progression and player-to-player trading through the physical Market.</p>
                    <div class="tc-tag-list">
                        <span>Physical Market</span>
                        <span>Dragon Balls</span>
                        <span>Meteors</span>
                        <span>Socketing</span>
                        <span>Player trading</span>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tc-section-heading mt-5">
            <div class="tc-kicker">PROJECT-SPECIFIC CONTENT</div>
            <h2>Selected additions that remain</h2>
            <p>These features are deliberate Placebo decisions rather than claims about the original 5017 patch.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="row tc-info-grid">
            <div class="col-md-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-custom">Custom</span>
                    <h3>Auto Hunt</h3>
                    <p>Modern quality of life with server-side permission gates and persisted VIP level.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-custom">Custom</span>
                    <h3>Lava Beast</h3>
                    <p>Retained by project decision and moved away from the disabled Frozen Grotto content.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 mb-4">
                <article class="tc-info-card">
                    <span class="tc-info-state tc-state-custom">Custom</span>
                    <h3>Launcher updates</h3>
                    <p>The adapted client can receive controlled incremental updates without changing the Era 1 gameplay target.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tc-era-note">
            <strong>About “5017 inspired”</strong>
            <p>Placebo uses an adapted 5695 client as its technical base. The server enforces the Era 1 gameplay boundary; selected later features are kept only when they are explicit project decisions.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="tc-cta">
    <div class="container text-center">
        <div class="tc-kicker">ENTER PLACEBO</div>
        <h2>Ready to play Era 1?</h2>
        <p>Get the client or read the guides before creating your first character.</p>
        <div class="tc-hero-actions justify-content-center">
            <a class="btn tc-btn-primary btn-lg" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Downloads">Download client</a>
            <a class="btn tc-btn-outline btn-lg" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Guides">Read guides</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
